 "notes": [
  "Engineering Solutions sold May 2, 2023; ES segment printed with zero for the quarter. Fincentric classified as held for sale at March 31, 2024 (BS assets 60, liabilities 10).",
  "IS \"Other (income) expense, net\" printed (9) -> oth_inc +9 (income); no non-GAAP adjustment to other income. Segment-table total expenses 2,106 = IS expenses 2,112 less equity income 6.",
  "CORP \"recovery of lease-related costs\" $1M ($1M after-tax) is a benefit -> pre -1 / net -1 (CORP items 18+2+1-1 = 20 = printed corp_nongaap).",
  "TAX items (footnote h): tax expense of $6M associated with IHS Markit prior to acquisition (+6), offset by tax benefit of $2M due to annualized effective tax rate differences for GAAP (-2).",
  "Item after-tax sum 55 = printed aggregate 55; 991 + 55 + 212 = 1,258.",
  "ngaap.items_total_pre = operating-level \"Non-GAAP adjustments\" (75); interest adjustment (premium amortization benefit, footnote g) printed separately as 7 (adjusted interest 85 vs GAAP 78).",
  "Segment rounding: MI 189+45+140=374 vs adj 373; Ratings 679+2+7=688 vs 687; CI 226+5+32=263 vs 264; Indices 272+2+9=283 vs 282; Corporate 57-20 = 37 vs adjusted 36.",
  "Non-GAAP adjusted tax line: non-GAAP adjustments 13, deal-related amortization 67.",
  "cfpub: capex and nci_dist (\"Distributions to noncontrolling interest holders, net\") positive outflows.",
  "Guidance raised: revenue growth 6.0%-8.0% (prior 5.5%-7.5%); GAAP EPS $10.80-$11.05; adjusted EPS $13.85-$14.10. Exhibit 8 bridge: deal amortization 2.77, IHS Markit merger costs 0.28, premium amortization benefit (0.07), restructuring 0.09, tax rate (0.02).",
  "No organic/constant-currency table; revenue ex Engineering Solutions growth 14% stated in text."
 ],
